          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is called
            %em compact
            if it is “finite” or “small” in some precise sense. There are however different formalizations of this idea. Here discussed is the notion, usually going by this term, where an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is called
            %em compact
            if mapping out of it
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+colimit"} preserves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          %p
            This means that if any other object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is given as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of a “suitably increasing” family of objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_i\}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X
                  \\longrightarrow
                  A
                  \=
                  \\underset{\underset{i}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim} A_i
          %p
            out of the compact object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into that colimit factors through one of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojections"} coprojections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi lim
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \to \underset{\underset{i}{\longrightarrow}}{lim A_i}
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
            is essentially the same, with a bit more flexibility on when the family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_i\}
            is taken to be “suitably increasing”. An important application of the above factorization property is accordingly named the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+object"} finite object
            (in a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %em
              %a{:href => "#SubtletiesAndDifferentMeanings"} Subtleties and different meanings
            below.
          %h2#FinitelyPresentableObject Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              that admits
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %strong compact
              %strong finitely presented
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %strong finitely presentable
              = succeed "," do
                %strong of finite presentation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corepresentable+functor"} corepresentable functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_C(X,-) \colon C \to Set
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
