                    is a
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+object"} coherent object
          %p
            However, there exist compact objects which are not coherent, c.f. the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                an object is compact precisely if it is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presented+group"} finitely presented
                as a group.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety+of+algebras"} variety of algebras
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presented+algebra"} finitely presented
                as an algebra. A proof may be found in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#AdamekRosicky94"} Adámek-Rosický 94, Corollary 3.13
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                and let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Op(X)
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
                is a compact object in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                precisely if it is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact topological space
                %em not
                true that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a compact object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                iff it is a compact topological space; see below.)
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional vector space
                is compact in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "finite-dimensional+vector+space#CompactClosure"} here
          %h2#SubtletiesAndDifferentMeanings Subtleties and different meanings
          %p One has to be careful about the following variations of the theme of compactness.
          %p
            (Some of these subtleties are resolved by noticing that there is a hierarchy of notions of compact objects that are secretly different but partly go by the same name. Some discussion of this is currently at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topos"} compact topos
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
            %em compact objects
            are those objects such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            element of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Sub}(C)
            is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+element"} compact element
            %em finitely-presented
            for the notion of compact on this page.
          %h3#CompactnessInAdditiveCategories Compactness in additive categories
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            (often a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is called
            %strong compact
            if for every set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such that the coproduct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{s\in S} s
            exists, the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\coprod_{s\in S} C(x,s)\to C(x,\coprod_{s\in S}s)
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoids
          %p Here is an application of this concept to characterize which abelian categories are categories of modules of some ring:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be an abelian category. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              and has a compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq R Mod
              for some ring
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = C(x,x)^{op}
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+projective+object"} compact projective
              generator. Conversely, if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq R Mod
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all small coproducts and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = R
              is a compact projective generator.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This theorem, minus the explicit description of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/reprints/articles/3/tr3.pdf#page=132"} Abelian Categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0506/0506603v1.pdf#page=4"} Lectures on noncommutative geometry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a compact projective generator of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
          .query
            %p
              Zoran: While Ginzburg’s reference is surely a worthy to look at, it would be better not to give false impression that this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstruction+theorem"} reconstruction theorem
              is due Ginzburg or at all new. It is rather a classical and well know fact probably from early 1960s, essentially small strengthening of a variant of a circle of abelian reconstruction theorems including the Gabriel-Popescu theorem(probably our variant could be read off from classical algera book by Faith for example, or Popescu’s book on abelian categories, in any case it is well known in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
          %p
            A triangulated category is
            %strong compactly generated
            if it is generated (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
            %em set
            of compact objects.
          %p
            The notion can be modified for categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            (compare to the notions of finite and/or rigid objects in various contexts).
          %p
            Compact objects in the derived categories of quasicoherent sheaves over a scheme are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+complexes"} perfect complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
            over a perfect ring is finitely generated as a module.
          %p
            In non-additive contexts, the above definition is not right. For instance, with this definition a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            would be compact iff it is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space"} connected
          %h3#CompactObjectsInTop
            Compact objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
          %p
            Recall the above example of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            if it is a compact object in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexample"} counterexample
            is given for instance in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), page 49
            %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Hovey/model-err.pdf"} errata
            of that book). See also the blog discussion
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/05/journal_club_geometric_infinit_3.html#c023790"} here
          %p
            Namely, the two-element set with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indiscrete+topology"} indiscrete topology
            is a compact space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for which
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom(X, -)
                  M\colon
                  Top \rightarrow Top
          %p
            doesn’t preserve filtered colimits, in fact not even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} colimits of sequences
            (functors out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} ordered set
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          %p For example, consider the sequence of spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_n=[n,\infty) \times \{0,1\}
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+sets"} open sets
            are of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [n, \infty] \times \{0\} \cup [m,\infty) \times \{1\}
          %p
            (where
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \geq n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \rightarrow X_{n+1}
            so that it sends a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k, \epsilon)
            to itself if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \gt n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,\epsilon)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1,\epsilon)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow Top
          %p
            The colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\infty
            of this sequence is the two-element set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            with the indiscrete topology. However, the identity map on this space does not factor through any of the canonical maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \rightarrow X_\infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi colim
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{n}{colim}\ Hom(X_\infty, X_n) \rightarrow Hom(X_\infty, X_\infty)
          %p is not surjective, and therefore not an isomorphism.
          .query
            %p
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd
              (posted from n-category cafe): I don’t know if the story is any different for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              compact
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hausdorff
          %p But with a bit of care on the assumptions, similar results do hold:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
